{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type HotkeySequence = Hotkey[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/sequence-manager.ts#L52","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sequence-manager.ts:52"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sequence of hotkeys for Vim-style shortcuts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each element is one step (a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hotkey"},{"type":"text","value":" string). Steps may include modifiers;\nthe same modifier can appear on consecutive steps (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+R"},{"type":"text","value":" then\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+T"},{"type":"text","value":"). Modifier-only key events do not advance or reset matching—see\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SequenceManager"},{"type":"text","value":". Automatic keydown repeats and IME composition are also ignored."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const gotoTop: HotkeySequence = ['G', 'G']  // gg\nconst deleteLine: HotkeySequence = ['D', 'D']  // dd\nconst deleteWord: HotkeySequence = ['D', 'I', 'W']  // diw\nconst chainedShift: HotkeySequence = ['Shift+R', 'Shift+T']","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype HotkeySequence = Hotkey[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [sequence-manager.ts:52](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/sequence-manager.ts#L52)\n\nA sequence of hotkeys for Vim-style shortcuts.\n\nEach element is one step (a `Hotkey` string). Steps may include modifiers;\nthe same modifier can appear on consecutive steps (e.g. `Shift+R` then\n`Shift+T`). Modifier-only key events do not advance or reset matching—see\n`SequenceManager`. Automatic keydown repeats and IME composition are also ignored.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst gotoTop: HotkeySequence = ['G', 'G']  // gg\nconst deleteLine: HotkeySequence = ['D', 'D']  // dd\nconst deleteWord: HotkeySequence = ['D', 'I', 'W']  // diw\nconst chainedShift: HotkeySequence = ['Shift+R', 'Shift+T']\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: HotkeySequence\ntitle: HotkeySequence\n---\n\n```ts\ntype HotkeySequence = Hotkey[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [sequence-manager.ts:52](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/sequence-manager.ts#L52)\n\nA sequence of hotkeys for Vim-style shortcuts.\n\nEach element is one step (a `Hotkey` string). Steps may include modifiers;\nthe same modifier can appear on consecutive steps (e.g. `Shift+R` then\n`Shift+T`). Modifier-only key events do not advance or reset matching—see\n`SequenceManager`. Automatic keydown repeats and IME composition are also ignored.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst gotoTop: HotkeySequence = ['G', 'G']  // gg\nconst deleteLine: HotkeySequence = ['D', 'D']  // dd\nconst deleteWord: HotkeySequence = ['D', 'I', 'W']  // diw\nconst chainedShift: HotkeySequence = ['Shift+R', 'Shift+T']\n```\n"}
